    {
      "vulnerability": {
        "@id": "https://ubuntu.com/security/notices/USN-9092-1",
        "name": "USN-9092-1",
        "description": "It was discovered that Cpanel::JSON::XS did not properly release memory when rejecting certain malformed JSON objects. An attacker could possibly use this issue to exhaust memory, resulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2026-110672)  It was discovered that Cpanel::JSON::XS did not properly limit nesting when decoding tagged values. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause applications using Cpanel::JSON::XS to crash, resulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2026-110673)  It was discovered that Cpanel::JSON::XS did not properly validate unquoted object keys when processing UTF-8 input. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause applications using Cpanel::JSON::XS to crash, resulting in a denial of service. This issue only affected Ubuntu 24.04 LTS, Ubuntu 26.04 LTS and Ubuntu 26.10. (CVE-2026-110675)  It was discovered that Cpanel::JSON::XS incorrectly handled numbers with large exponents when arbitrary precision number support was enabled. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause excessive memory and processor consumption, resulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2026-110676)  It was discovered that Cpanel::JSON::XS did not properly release memory when collecting duplicate object key values into arrays. An attacker could possibly use this issue to exhaust memory, resulting in a denial of service. This issue only affected Ubuntu 24.04 LTS, Ubuntu 26.04 LTS and Ubuntu 26.10. (CVE-2026-110677)  It was discovered that Cpanel::JSON::XS did not properly enforce input size limits when parsing JSON incrementally. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to exhaust memory, resulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2026-110678)  It was discovered that Cpanel::JSON::XS incorrectly handled memory when encoding certain objects with sorted keys. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause applications using Cpanel::JSON::XS to crash, resulting in a denial of service. This issue only affected Ubuntu 22.04 LTS, Ubuntu 24.04 LTS, Ubuntu 26.04 LTS and Ubuntu 26.10. (CVE-2026-110680)  It was discovered that Cpanel::JSON::XS incorrectly handled memory when parser objects were copied between threads. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause applications using Cpanel::JSON::XS to crash, resulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2026-110681)  It was discovered that Cpanel::JSON::XS incorrectly handled top-level values when parsing JSON incrementally. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to alter the number and contents of messages interpreted by an application by controlling how input was split across reads. This issue only affected Ubuntu 26.10. (CVE-2026-110682)  It was discovered that Cpanel::JSON::XS did not properly release memory when encoding certain values as strings. An attacker could possibly use this issue to exhaust memory, resulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2026-110684)  It was discovered that Cpanel::JSON::XS did not properly release memory when errors occurred while decoding tagged values. An attacker could possibly use this issue to exhaust memory, resulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2026-110685)",
        "aliases": [
          "CVE-2026-110672",
          "CVE-2026-110673",
